{
  "algorithm": "HPKE",
  "schema": "hpke_decrypt_test_schema.json",
  "numberOfTests": 4,
  "header": [
    "Test vectors for HPKE (RFC 9180) Open of a message SEQUENCE in base",
    "mode using the ML-KEM-1024 KEM from draft-ietf-hpke-pq. HPKE Open is",
    "stateful and ordered: SetupBaseR once, then Open each message with",
    "AEAD nonce base_nonce XOR sequenceNumber. Each case carries one enc",
    "and an ordered list of decryptions, covering nonce evolution and",
    "rejection of out-of-order, replayed, and skipped ciphertexts. See",
    "doc/hpke.md."
  ],
  "notes": {
    "MultiMessage": {
      "bugType": "FUNCTIONALITY",
      "description": "A sequence of messages opened in order on one HPKE context. Each Open advances the sequence number, so the AEAD nonce is base_nonce XOR sequenceNumber; opening the messages in order MUST recover each plaintext."
    },
    "OutOfOrderCiphertext": {
      "bugType": "AUTH_BYPASS",
      "description": "A ciphertext sealed at one sequence number is presented at a different one, so the AEAD nonce (base_nonce XOR sequenceNumber) does not match the one used to seal; Open MUST fail at the tag check."
    },
    "ReplayedCiphertext": {
      "bugType": "AUTH_BYPASS",
      "description": "A ciphertext already opened at its sequence number is replayed at a later sequence number; the nonce differs, so Open MUST fail. HPKE contexts do not accept a message twice."
    },
    "SkippedSequenceNumber": {
      "bugType": "AUTH_BYPASS",
      "description": "A ciphertext sealed for a later sequence number is opened after skipping one or more sequence numbers; the nonce does not match, so Open MUST fail."
    }
  },
